id: pm-ado-sparse-refresh
title: Compile sparse Azure refresh plans with explicit field accounting
description: "Overlap rechecked: sync.ts owns transport batching and three-way field reconciliation; core list output budgets shape local output; pm-jira search projections and pm-linear GraphQL selection own different provider protocols. This adds a read-only, reviewable, costed refresh compiler using saved Azure revisions/bases and declared pm field needs."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T21:50:36.590Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T15:11:09.891Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "A 1000-item fixture uses at most five batch reads per refresh phase; unchanged items cause zero pm mutations; every requested field is accounted for; unavailable rows never become deletions. Typed SDK and CLI, compact output, typed remedies, no-git real tracker validation, seeded property and boundary tests, unchanged release gates."
comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T21:54:35.625Z",codex-agent,"Implemented read-only compileRefreshPlan and observeRefreshPlan plus ado refresh-plan. Uses certified listAllComplete reads, existing Azure batchIds and AdoClient transport, and the existing field map/base reader. Fresh revision probes distinguish exact matches from unavailable rows. Artifacts contain read requests only, no journal, idempotency keys, apply path, status-name inference or shared mutable state. Foreign/unlinked records are skipped with counted reasons. Testing strict schema boundaries, 1000-item costs, SDK readback and real non-git trackers next."
  "2026-10-25T22:00:02.728Z",codex-agent,"Model-based acceptance passed: 500 seeded import/export/sync sequences with SDK-read reference state, CRLF/whitespace variants, all mapped native fields, custom active/blocked/done/canceled/draft statuses, hierarchy and related edges, exact replays and older-input refusals. Found and fixed older-revision rollback in existing sync. Terminal transitions now use SDK registry roles. Additional 500 seeded refresh sequences cover accounting/omissions/extreme revisions. Six competing transitions at every async observation boundary preserve peer writes. Read-only public main tracker copy: 32 items, 69 authoritative files hash-identical; unchanged projection 1 probe/0 hydration, all-changed 1/1 and 288 cells; mixed 17 unchanged, 8 changed, 7 unavailable, 72 cells; complete JSON 1095/1419/1351 bytes. Synthetic Azure evidence only; no live Azure credential validation."
  "2026-10-25T22:03:03.947Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: forcing eager hydration in compileRefreshPlan makes the 1000-item regression fail (5 hydration reads versus required 0 for unchanged rows). Replacing only runSyncCommand with its main implementation makes the older-revision regression fail because import succeeds instead of refusing. Restored implementations pass both targeted regressions (2/2). New refresh.ts targeted V8 coverage is 100% lines/branches/functions; full unchanged-threshold npm and Bun release gates will run in CI."
  "2026-10-25T22:07:22.399Z",codex-agent,"Open-PR overlap reviewed: PR 46 owns SDK-guarded sync mutations and remote-effect recovery/outboxes, not sparse refresh compilation. This branch remains based on main as requested and adds no journal or mutation executor. Its two small sync repairs cover older-revision refusal and terminal registry roles discovered by the required model tests; integration with PR 46 may need source conflict resolution after either branch lands. Local normal-home health sees an unrelated global pm-github host-version skew; isolated-home strict health passes. No global extension or telemetry configuration was changed."
  "2026-10-25T22:07:24.100Z",codex-agent,"The linked targeted suite exceeded pm test default 120 seconds; rerunning with an explicit 600-second allowance. The first run also caught invalid fractional saved revisions being misclassified as stale conflicts; the new rollback guard now applies only to valid integer revisions, preserving the existing usage-refusal contract. Test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so command results are recorded here and in PR evidence rather than enabling tracking."
  "2026-10-25T22:08:33.248Z",codex-agent,"Linked targeted verification passed: node --test test/refresh.test.ts test/sync.test.ts via pm test --run --progress --timeout 600: 59/59, zero failures/cancellations/skips, 142 seconds. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint (97 documented declarations), whitespace check and isolated-home strict health pass. Added full SDK readback of both model targets and mode-count diagnostics for final CI. Final npm/Bun release gates are delegated to the existing CI matrix at unchanged thresholds to avoid another local full-gate run on the saturated host. Remaining validation boundary: synthetic Azure REST contract, no live credentials."
  "2026-10-25T22:11:55.361Z",codex-agent,"First CI run 40238883034 failed in the newly strengthened reference relationship assertion: it compared SDK-generated creation timestamps between independently created trackers. Correcting the assertion to compare owned id/kind/source_kind semantics; preserving an explicit invariant that the actual stored relationship timestamp/author metadata matches its original SDK readback, alongside byte-identical exact replay checks. No production behavior or coverage threshold is weakened."
  "2026-10-25T22:15:51.654Z",codex-agent,"Corrected reference-model rerun passes all 500 sequences: 181 imports, 152 exports, 167 syncs, 500 exact replays and 50 older-input replays. SDK readback now checks both targets, models symmetric related-link materialization at the next import, compares owned edge semantics across independent trackers, and preserves each actual edge creation record against its original SDK readback. Exact command: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"500 seeded import/export/sync\" test/sync.test.ts (1/1, 88 seconds, zero skips). Initial CI failure was a test oracle error; production code and all thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-25T22:20:57.031Z",codex-agent,"Verified gate receipt for ff063cf72f39e8c985cc880c58d55e96591bc43e: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40239448954 passed 4/4 jobs (Node 22, Node 26, npm release gate, Bun release gate). Each job passed 239/239 tests in both V8 and independent Istanbul runs, zero failures/skips; 1504/1504 statements, 100% statements/lines/branches/functions across all nine required sources. CodeQL run 40239448838 passed. Overlap was also verified against installed CLI 2026.10.25 list projection/read-output-budget declarations and current Jira/Linear main provider code. Ready PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/48 . This final evidence-only commit records the verified source/test head; final pushed-head checks remain linked from the PR. No new core CLI/SDK defects were discovered beyond the documented local environment/version-skew and existing disabled test-result persistence policy. No merge or release performed."
  "2026-10-26T04:31:58.295Z",codex-agent,"Review continuation: closing SDK-acquisition class. Host context supplies PmClient schema queries, so import/export/sync will use ctx.sdk.client only and query roles lazily when a status changes. The pinned context does not expose low-level history/lease primitives needed by resolution; standalone service callers will inject their SDK explicitly, while resolution commands use only the documented pm-install host SDK link with a canonical module anchor and typed refusal. Delete argv-based loader fallback. Add packed install-shape acceptance in isolated temporary prefixes, retaining all previous sparse-compiler evidence."
  "2026-10-26T04:44:20.974Z",codex-agent,"Initial packed acceptance passed 7/7 (matrix parent plus six launch shapes), including 24/24 import/export/sync/refresh commands, SDK-read lifecycle/revision checks, and lazy resolution-plan smoke checks. All fixtures use isolated HOME/npm/Bun caches and prefixes and no git executable. Strengthened copied-extension regression removes only SDK links created inside its own temporary tracker: these four commands must remain functional, while resolution must refuse with a typed installation remedy. Running the pre-fix acquisition functions against that regression for behavioral revert proof. The unit fixture also exposed SDK 2026.10.23 preview rejecting SDK dependency symlinks inside tracker storage; no upstream or SDK pin change is made."
  "2026-10-26T04:48:49.748Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof confirmed with the strengthened packed test: restoring only the previous sync/resolution acquisition functions and rebuilding makes the copied-extension npm-global-symlink import return ADO_REMOTE (exit 3, empty plans) before tracker reconciliation. Other five install shapes pass, isolating the missing-module-link/launcher-path class. Source and build restored. The final matrix will also verify that client-only commands succeed without the module link and resolution returns its explicit installation remedy."
  "2026-10-26T04:50:46.701Z",codex-agent,"Review acceptance added without changing original criteria: six packed launch shapes (npm global symlink, Bun global bin, npx, bunx, local node_modules bin, and another tracker installed with pm install) must each pass import/export/sync/refresh on a non-git tracker. Client-only commands must not require any SDK module link. Resolution must use canonical installed peer resolution lazily and give a typed remedy when unavailable; standalone callers inject the SDK explicitly. Preserve temporary-prefix cleanup, declared status roles, unchanged release thresholds, and the prior 1000-item, state-model, field-accounting and unavailable-row evidence."
  "2026-10-26T04:55:54.486Z",codex-agent,"Final packed acceptance through pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress --timeout 900 passed 7/7, 24/24 required command runs, zero test skips/failures; six isolated install shapes with CLI 2026.10.25, SDK state readback, no git executable, cleanup of private prefixes/caches. Copied-extension commands also succeed after removing only fixture-owned SDK module links; resolution then gives a typed configuration/install remedy and invalid selections avoid loading it. Focused command/state checks pass 4/4; typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint (97 declarations) and whitespace checks pass. One matrix setup iteration needed priming npm exec registry metadata before offline invocations; corrected without relaxing assertions. Revert proof is recorded above. Full npm/Bun gates will verify this repair in CI at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-26T05:02:55.364Z",codex-agent,"While CI runners were queued, focused coverage verified the changed resolution module: 18/18 tests, zero skips/failures, 100% lines/branches/functions. Added a valid read-only plan without a mutation author so lazy loading and the existing author fallback are tested after selection validation. Exact command: node --test --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=resolution.ts --test-name-pattern=\"resolution|portable choices|remote field choices\" test/sync.test.ts . This is a test-only addition; production repair remains unchanged. Superseded queued CI runs are not counted as evidence; the final pushed head must pass npm/Bun gates."
  "2026-10-26T14:16:46.706Z",codex-agent,"Re-review continuation: restore additive public API compatibility. Preserve the documented five-argument AdoResolutionService constructor, optional explicit SDK/observer forms and every other prior exported call form. Audit declaration diffs; acquire a default SDK only when omitted using the canonical package import path, never launcher discovery. Add an immutable previous-API consumer compiled/run against built code plus an exported declaration snapshot gate. Keep prior install-shape, sparse refresh and state evidence; add constructor-required behavioral revert proof and unchanged CI npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-26T14:54:50.241Z",codex-agent,"Published API audit against npm pm-ado 2026.10.26 is complete: five prior declaration modules retain their call forms. Restored optional SDK/observer construction and exported loadResolutionSdk(anchors?). The only pre-existing signature addition is optional batch projection; its default also preserves runtime arity 1. Constructor/loader runtime arities remain 5/0, verified against released JavaScript. Legacy fixture covers 35 value names, 32 type names, five constructor forms, one-argument reads and loader anchors; same source compiles with published and built declarations, runs built JS under Node and Bun, and reads real non-git SDK state without git on PATH. Complete built declaration snapshots cover six modules. Revert proof: making only the SDK parameter mandatory and rebuilding fails the consumer with TS2554/TS2345 and fails the snapshot; removing the loader declaration fails TS2305 and the snapshot. Restored gates pass 2/2. Focused resolution tests pass 18/18 with 100% lines/branches/functions."
  "2026-10-26T15:00:25.482Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility gates pass through pinned pm test (2/2, zero test skips/failures), including Node+Bun execution with no git executable and cleanup of isolated tracker homes. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint (97 declarations), whitespace and fixture privacy checks pass. The immutable baseline is npm pm-ado 2026.10.26 with integrity/archive/declaration/documentation hashes; no binary or cache is tracked. CI automatically includes the new public-api tests in both release-gate runs; snapshots are never auto-updated by CI. Prior sparse-refresh, model-based and install-shape work remains intact; no SDK dependency pin changed."
  "2026-10-26T15:10:31.539Z",codex-agent,"Integrated the current main base to resolve GitHub mergeability after the compatibility fix. The only conflict was the generated index source map, rebuilt from the auto-merged TypeScript. Preserved incoming release metadata and toolchain changes; retained the pinned SDK. Rechecking the combined build before a fresh CI release gate."
  "2026-10-26T15:11:07.722Z",codex-agent,"Combined-base targeted checks pass: typecheck, test compilation, docstring gate (97 declarations), and public API consumer/snapshot (2/2). Local strict tracker health has one pre-existing extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew for pm-github (pinned host 2026.10.23 versus local extension 2026.10.25); storage, integrity and history drift pass. No SDK pin or local extension changes are included; fresh CI checkout health remains required."
